WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Liquid ai's D1.2 models read text, images and audio, then return calibrated probabilities with zero output tokens. This is Models &amp; Agents Episode 237. Sarvam stood up India-hosted inference, Simon Willison published External Sandbox prototypes, and Google tracked agents writing exploits from patches, then things to try. Liquid ai, Mark Tech Post reports released D1.2 and D1.2 Ultra as Omni-modal decision models built for task.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.900
where probability distribution is more useful than generated text.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:40.420
D1.2 ultra-lands at 75 on artificial analysis decision index version 2.1.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:44.940
Risks scoring, routing and verification pipelines can hit one endpoint

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.080
and get well-calibrated numbers across modalities.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.540
Three distinct input types go through one forward pass

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:56.220
and come back as numeric outputs only, which cuts token generation overhead.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:05.692
India hosted GPU clusters at Sarvam Token Factory, now runs Sarvam 105B, GLM 5.3, Deepseek

00:01:05.692 --> 00:01:13.792
V4.1 Flash, KimiK 3.1 Pro, and Gemma 4.31B, through one open AI compatible API.

00:01:14.432 --> 00:01:19.272
The platform is open to everyone and routes requests to eight distinct open models on domestic

00:01:19.272 --> 00:01:20.132
infrastructure.

00:01:20.912 --> 00:01:25.872
Developers get an alternative endpoint that skips US or European providers, while keeping

00:01:25.872 --> 00:01:28.912
Keeping the same request format used with open AI clients.

00:01:29.372 --> 00:01:34.352
Multiple model families sit under one set of credentials in billing, so latency and cost

00:01:34.352 --> 00:01:37.472
line up against each other on an identical API surface.

00:01:38.192 --> 00:01:43.072
Early users can exercise both dense and mixture of experts' architectures without changing

00:01:43.072 --> 00:01:43.852
client code.

00:01:44.845 --> 00:01:49.745
Simon Willison and Prime Radiant published an index repository on GitHub for the external

00:01:49.745 --> 00:01:55.025
sandbox prototypes, collecting multiple sandbox server implementations developed with the

00:01:55.025 --> 00:01:57.205
AI Research Lab behind superpowers.

00:01:57.625 --> 00:02:00.285
Each implementation shows credential isolation

00:02:00.285 --> 00:02:03.225
and proxy patterns, and you can clone the repo

00:02:03.225 --> 00:02:05.945
to inspect working examples of network restricted

00:02:05.945 --> 00:02:07.945
credential-free agent runtimes.

00:02:08.425 --> 00:02:10.365
The work aims at practical deployment

00:02:10.365 --> 00:02:12.445
rather than new research abstractions.

00:02:13.375 --> 00:02:15.275
A post on R-slash machine learning

00:02:15.275 --> 00:02:17.575
collects a reading order covering Horavod,

00:02:18.075 --> 00:02:22.215
PyTorch Distributed, Zero, Megatron LM, G-Pipe,

00:02:22.215 --> 00:02:38.055
and PyTorch FSDP for anyone building distributed training frameworks from first principles, video lectures on building a distributed training framework come first, then papers that establish splitting work across data, splitting the model itself, and cutting memory use.

00:02:38.635 --> 00:02:48.935
Every resource points to the original papers or implementations so readers can follow the progression without searching, and the list is for people who want the internals rather than high level APIs.

00:02:49.675 --> 00:02:53.455
Contributors can suggest reordering or additions directly in the thread.

00:02:54.381 --> 00:03:00.941
In a quicker pass, Google researchers observed attackers automating the whole vulnerability discovery and exploitation loop

00:03:00.941 --> 00:03:08.221
with multi-agent frameworks that perform patch-diffing, generate exploit candidates and test them with no human intervention.

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:13.761
The new stack reports and a publicly exposed staging server held the exploit agent framework

00:03:13.761 --> 00:03:18.921
besides stolen victim data and scripts for reconnaissance, brute force attacks, and

00:03:18.921 --> 00:03:23.881
web shell installation, with operators looking at French media, entertainment, and education

00:03:23.881 --> 00:03:27.661
websites and at access controls in the Spectra WordPress plugin.

00:03:28.321 --> 00:03:33.121
Karen, in the Google Threat Intelligence Group report published Monday as covered by the hacker

00:03:33.121 --> 00:03:42.781
news, targeted US Aerospace Organizations with an Observe-Orient Decide Act Loop, and a

00:03:42.781 --> 00:03:47.681
patch-diffing work autonomously, and other frameworks following similar orchestration around

00:03:47.681 --> 00:03:49.261
open source offensive tooling.

00:03:49.761 --> 00:03:55.501
Open AI is expanding free access to frontier models for up to 200,000 scientists worldwide

00:03:55.501 --> 00:04:01.401
with training and support, building on an earlier pilot among more than 1,800 participants

00:04:01.401 --> 00:04:06.801
who reported nearly doubling their output when using chat GPT across idea development, data

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:12.501
analysis and code writing, and privacy preserving analysis showed usage from initial ideation

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:14.421
through Final Manuscript Preparation.

00:04:15.061 --> 00:04:20.301
Chat GPT for health care now includes more capable computer use agents, stronger clinical

00:04:20.301 --> 00:04:26.461
answers, and more than 20 new health care plugins used by Average, Ambience AI, SIGNA, and

00:04:26.461 --> 00:04:31.901
CBS Health for prior authorizations, referrals, discharge planning, and patient outreach.

00:04:32.421 --> 00:04:37.521
With those agents navigating existing clinical systems on behalf of care teams, and connecting

00:04:37.521 --> 00:04:41.761
providing medical evidence to tools already in daily use inside hospitals and insurers.

00:04:42.685 --> 00:04:47.705
Call the Sarvim Token Factory endpoint with one hosted model and compare latency and

00:04:47.705 --> 00:04:51.385
cost against the open AI compatible provider you already use.

00:04:51.885 --> 00:04:58.225
Run the Liquid AI D1.2 decision model on a multi-modal verification task and see how probability

00:04:58.225 --> 00:05:00.665
outputs change downstream routing logic.

00:05:01.205 --> 00:05:06.165
Review the distributed training reading list on our slash machine learning if you are scaling

00:05:06.165 --> 00:05:12.665
training jobs beyond a single node. Applications for that scientist access program opened November 23rd

00:05:12.665 --> 00:05:19.254
and shared data is not used for training by default. California's lawsuit over AI agent sandbox

00:05:19.254 --> 00:05:25.274
escapes is expected to draw further state level responses. Further plugins and computer use agent

00:05:25.274 --> 00:05:31.408
updates are expected in that chat GPT for healthcare offering. Let me pop the hood on those external

00:05:31.408 --> 00:05:36.168
sandboxes, because the design decision is to keep the agent's own credentials outside

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:37.528
the execution environment.

00:05:38.328 --> 00:05:43.488
Untrusted code running inside never sees keys, and it cannot touch agent configs or logs.

00:05:44.388 --> 00:05:49.348
Operators shrink the blast radius of a compromise by putting identity material on one side of that

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.768
boundary and the guest process on the other.

00:05:52.408 --> 00:05:58.128
Configuration files and execution logs stay on the host, so a sandbox process cannot read or

00:05:58.128 --> 00:05:58.868
overwrite them.

00:05:58.868 --> 00:06:03.948
The complete network disablement inside the sandbox is workable because the model endpoint

00:06:03.948 --> 00:06:09.268
is reached through a host side HTTP proxy rather than direct outbound sockets.

00:06:09.708 --> 00:06:14.628
That proxy can enforce host allow lists and do credential replacement, so model calls

00:06:14.628 --> 00:06:17.468
still go through while the guest stays off the open network.

00:06:18.068 --> 00:06:22.568
The same pattern supports running thousands of sandboxes on a single host without copying

00:06:22.568 --> 00:06:24.508
credentials into every container image.

00:06:24.508 --> 00:06:29.768
The engineering rule is to use it for network restricted credential-free agent runtimes

00:06:29.768 --> 00:06:34.508
at high density on one machine, and not to use it when a model call has to leave through

00:06:34.508 --> 00:06:37.508
a direct outbound socket instead of the host side proxy.

00:06:38.423 --> 00:06:43.063
Before we go, new server implementations that extend the proxy and isolation patterns

00:06:43.063 --> 00:06:46.703
are what that external sandbox repository is poised to add next.

